{"skill":{"slug":"rss-ai-reader","displayName":"Rss Ai Reader"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770023411548,"changelog":"- 首次发布 RSS AI 阅读器：自动抓取 RSS/Atom 订阅，利用 Claude/OpenAI 生成中文摘要，并多渠道推送（飞书、Telegram、Email）。\n- 配置简单，支持定时任务和 SQLite 去重，避免重复推送。\n- 命令行支持单次执行、定时任务和查看统计信息。\n- 详细文档与配置示例，便于快速上手。","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2786,"sha256":"0abcc8438f644cdb56866a3000c6966577a5531f6157c874b06a2fce5c154f00","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/config_guide.md","size":2472,"sha256":"8a0eae0de6acc1d59c276823849d310e7b84620ad345a204285529cc1e4c03d4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2193,"sha256":"506d11f8f15759a6f8e3b6c32c040076e34d0e10ad5dff70481f25390c358738","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789028138824,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"fd069095ad4e18d8212cb1780d618c76e53c70083b2ba80194ffe1dfa24355ec","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/fd069095ad4e18d8212cb1780d618c76e53c70083b2ba80194ffe1dfa24355ec","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: rss-ai-reader\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill instructs the agent to clone and execute code from an external GitHub repository (https://github.com/BENZEMA216/rss-reader.git) via `git clone` and `pip install -r requirements.txt` commands in `SKILL.md`. This introduces a significant supply chain risk, as the actual code being run is not part of the analyzed bundle. Additionally, the skill is designed to handle multiple sensitive API keys and passwords (for LLMs, Feishu, Telegram, and Email SMTP) as environment variables or in configuration files, as detailed in `SKILL.md` and `references/config_guide.md`, increasing the potential attack surface for credential compromise if the external code were malicious.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160849041},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":44,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789028138824},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This RSS summarizer is purpose-aligned, but it asks users to install and run unpinned code from an external GitHub repository while using API keys and notification credentials.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The workflow can expose feed contents, summaries, LLM API keys, webhooks, bot tokens, and email credentials to local runtime code and third-party services without strong disclosure or containment guidance.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The quick start clones the current default branch of an external GitHub repository and installs requirements from it, so the reviewed skill package does not contain or pin the code users are asked to run.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Most triggers fit RSS/news monitoring, but phrases like generic site monitoring and daily news pushes are broad enough that activation boundaries should be tightened.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill supports a long-running scheduled mode and a local SQLite database for deduplication, but it does not show system service installation, privilege escalation, or hidden persistence.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is coherent: fetch RSS/Atom feeds, summarize with Claude/OpenAI, deduplicate with SQLite, and send notifications through Feishu, Telegram, or Email.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review or pin the GitHub repository before installing, run it in a virtual environment or container under a non-admin account, provide only the credentials needed for enabled channels, and avoid feeding it sensitive private RSS content unless you are comfortable with the LLM and notification providers receiving that data.","findings":"[T03] unexpected: The static finding is supported by the artifact: SKILL.md instructs users to clone and run a mutable external repository without a reviewed commit, release signature, or vendored code.\n[SQP-1] expected: The broad trigger language is mostly related to RSS and news monitoring, but it should be narrowed to explicit feed-management intent to reduce unexpected invocation.\n[SQP-2] expected: Using Claude/OpenAI and notification services is central to the advertised function, but the artifact under-discloses the privacy and credential-handling implications.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese summaries and Chinese documentation appear consistent with the presented audience; this is a usability and disclosure note, not a security escalation by itself.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789028138824}}}}}